                        "sense_id": "c7c818ad-2460-39d3-8208-7a123dbd014a",
                        "entry_id": "60148ac2-c902-3115-90cc-550a04c112b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of something that wells, or issues forth like water."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "070a7857-f0dc-43ae-b43b-86f50b7c843a",
                                "sense_id": "c7c818ad-2460-39d3-8208-7a123dbd014a",
                                "text": "It spread slowly up from the sea-rim, a welling upwards of pure white light, ghosting the beach with silver and drawing the grey bastions of sandstone out of formless space."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b377789a-38d4-406c-b359-f1d64d58f715",
                                "sense_id": "c7c818ad-2460-39d3-8208-7a123dbd014a",
                                "text": "Later experience suggested that such wellings up of molten glass from caverns filled with active lava in a period of outflow might be due to sudden generation of steam from cascades of water during torrential rainfall."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
